Wait — guard insert: if first succeeds and second fails, we throw → transaction rolls back → first guard insert also rolled back. Good.

But ordering: insert transfer first to get id, then guards. If guard fails → ConflictException → rollback removes the transfer row too. Good.

Hmm, one subtlety: the idempotency_record insert happens in same tx, so on rollback it's removed too — consistent with existing style (failures don't leave idempotency records; retry allowed).

